# Home server deploys

The always-on box is `ssh kuro`. Utility lives in `/srv/utility`. Compose project `utility`, ports `18100–18199`. Kuro (the voice/n8n project) stays out of this stack.

`utility-deploy.timer` already runs `deploy/scripts/deploy.sh` every 2 minutes. That script fetches `origin/main`, waits until GitHub checks are green, migrates, rebuilds, and health-gates. It resets the checkout to `origin/main`, so uncommitted files on the server are wiped.

## When server or deploy code changes

Do the rollout yourself. Do not tell the user to pull, migrate, or rebuild.

1. `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, and `npm run test` must exit 0.
2. Commit and push to `main` (this rule is the standing ask to ship those changes).
3. `deploy/scripts/deploy.sh` must stay executable in git (`100755`). systemd runs that path directly, and a `644` file fails the timer with status 203.
4. `ssh kuro 'systemctl start utility-deploy.service'` and read the journal until the log says `success` or names a CI/health failure. If the unit cannot start, run `bash /srv/utility/app/deploy/scripts/deploy.sh` as `kuro`.
4. If checks are still pending, wait and start the unit again. Do not bypass the CI gate in `deploy.sh`.

Vercel still publishes the Next.js app from the GitHub push. The SSH step is only for the home-server image, migration, and file host.
